    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "afc5400f_760c58f4",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/IBluetoothSocketCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1928656
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-24T23:35:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In AOSP CHRE, verifying that the endpoint (a nanoapp) exists on the MCU and can accept the offloaded socket requires changing thread context from the message thread to CHRE\u0027s thread, which is the reason for the async response. I think ensuring that an endpoint accepts a socket should be part of the \"open\" contract.\n\nI could also see this being useful for implementations that may need to send something from the MCU to the BT controller and wait for a response to accept a socket.",
      "parentUuid": "0c6bf4b7_89a8312e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 29,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "4ba8aa28cc934ff69d1503e59696c2ceae62b1c2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "95a159d1_b1c2901a",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/IBluetoothSocketCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-24T23:41:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e verifying that the endpoint (a nanoapp) exists on the MCU and can accept the\n\u003e offloaded socket requires changing thread context from the message thread to\n\u003e CHRE\u0027s thread,\n\nValidating this information should be done synchronously I believe, implementing a command where parameter validation is deferred feels wrong. If this does not take too long you should be able to block in the binder thread waiting for the validation to be complete, i.e. the cost of async validation should not be pushed to the caller (the host stack).\n\n\u003e I could also see this being useful for implementations that may need to send \n\u003e something from the MCU to the BT controller and wait for a response to accept a \n\u003e socket.\n\nThe socket has already been accepted at this point (wrt to the internal l2cap exchanges). Assuming we don\u0027t have a concrete use case yet, I would prefer to defer adding this API to a later bump.",
      "parentUuid": "afc5400f_760c58f4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 29,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "4ba8aa28cc934ff69d1503e59696c2ceae62b1c2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
